:[]},{"span":{"Deduplicated":1331},"id":54005,"kind":{"StorageDead":38},"comments_before":[]},{"span":{"Deduplicated":1331},"id":54006,"kind":{"StorageDead":37},"comments_before":[]},{"span":{"Deduplicated":1331},"id":54007,"kind":{"StorageDead":36},"comments_before":[]},{"span":{"Deduplicated":1331},"id":54008,"kind":{"StorageDead":35},"comments_before":[]},{"span":{"Deduplicated":1331},"id":46201,"kind":"Return","comments_before":[]}]},"comments":[]}}},{"def_id":40,"item_meta":{"name":[{"Ident":["core",0]},{"Ident":["slice",0]},{"Impl":{"Ty":{"params":{"regions":[],"types":[{"index":0,"name":"T","variance":"Unknown"}],"const_generics":[],"trait_clauses":[],"outlives":[],"trait_type_constraints":[]},"skip_binder":{"Deduplicated":8},"kind":"InherentImplBlock"}}},{"Ident":["sort_unstable",0]}],"span":{"Untagged":{"data":{"file_id":3,"beg":{"line":3150,"col":4},"end":{"line":3152,"col":15}},"generated_from_span":null}},"source_text":null,"attr_info":{"attributes":[{"DocComment":" Sorts the slice in ascending order **without** preserving the initial order of equal elements."},{"DocComment":""},{"DocComment":" This sort is unstable (i.e., may reorder equal elements), in-place (i.e., does not"},{"DocComment":" allocate), and *O*(*n* \\* log(*n*)) worst-case."},{"DocComment":""},{"DocComment":" If the implementation of [`Ord`] for `T` does not implement a [total order], the function"},{"DocComment":" may panic; even if the function exits normally, the resulting order of elements in the slice"},{"DocComment":" is unspecified. See also the note on panicking below."},{"DocComment":""},{"DocComment":" For example `|a, b| (a - b).cmp(a)` is a comparison function that is neither transitive nor"},{"DocComment":" reflexive nor total, `a < b < c < a` with `a = 1, b = 2, c = 3`. For more information and"},{"DocComment":" examples see the [`Ord`] documentation."},{"DocComment":""},{"DocComment":""},{"DocComment":" All original elements will remain in the slice and any possible modifications via interior"},{"DocComment":" mutability are observed in the input. Same is true if the implementation of [`Ord`] for `T` panics."},{"DocComment":""},{"DocComment":" Sorting types that only implement [`PartialOrd`] such as [`f32`] and [`f64`] require"},{"DocComment":" additional precautions. For example, `f32::NAN != f32::NAN`, which doesn't fulfill the"},{"DocComment":" reflexivity requirement of [`Ord`]. By using an alternative comparison function with"},{"DocComment":" `slice::sort_unstable_by` such as [`f32::total_cmp`] or [`f64::total_cmp`] that defines a"},{"DocComment":" [total order] users can sort slices containing floating-point values. Alternatively, if all"},{"DocComment":" values in the slice are guaranteed to be in a subset for which [`PartialOrd::partial_cmp`]"},{"DocComment":" forms a [total order], it's possible to sort the slice with `sort_unstable_by(|a, b|"},{"DocComment":" a.partial_cmp(b).unwrap())`."},{"DocComment":""},{"DocComment":" # Current implementation"},{"DocComment":""},{"DocComment":" The current implementation is based on [ipnsort] by Lukas Bergdoll and Orson Peters, which"},{"DocComment":" combines the fast average case of quicksort with the fast worst case of heapsort, achieving"},{"DocComment":" linear time on fully sorted and reversed inputs. On inputs with k distinct elements, the"},{"DocComment":" expected time to sort the data is *O*(*n* \\* log(*k*))."},{"DocComment":""},{"DocComment":" It is typically faster than stable sorting, except in a few special cases, e.g., when the"},{"DocComment":" slice is partially sorted."},{"DocComment":""},{"DocComment":" # Panics"},{"DocComment":""},{"DocComment":" May panic if the implementation of [`Ord`] for `T` does not implement a [total order], or if"},{"DocComment":" the [`Ord`] implementation panics."},{"DocComment":""},{"DocComment":" # Examples"},{"DocComment":""},{"DocComment":" ```"},{"DocComment":" let mut v = [4, -5, 1, -3, 2];"},{"DocComment":""},{"DocComment":" v.sort_unstable();"},{"DocComment":" assert_eq!(v, [-5, -3, 1, 2, 4]);"},{"DocComment":" ```"},{"DocComment":""},{"DocComment":" [ipnsort]: https://github.com/Voultapher/sort-research-rs/tree/main/ipnsort"},{"DocComment":" [total order]: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Total_order"}],"inline":"Hint","rename":null,"public":true},"is_local":false,"started_from":false,"is_extern":false,"opacity":"Foreign","lang_item":null,"diagnostic_item":null,"has_errors":false},"generics":{"regions":[{"index":0,"name":null,"variance":"Covariant","mutability":"Unknown","late_bound":true}],"types":[{"index":0,"name":"T","variance":"Unknown"}],"const_generics":[],"trait_clauses":[{"clause_id":0,"span":{"Value":[1349,{"data":{"file_id":3,"beg":{"line":3152,"col":11},"end":{"line":3152,"col":14}},"generated_from_span":null}]},"origin":"WhereClauseOnFn","trait_":{"regions":[],"outlives":[],"skip_binder":{"id":9,"generics":{"regions":[],"types":[{"Deduplicated":15}],"const_generics":[],"trait_refs":[]}}}}],"outlives":[{"regions":[],"outlives":[],"skip_binder":[{"Lub":{"Deduplicated":15}},{"Var":{"Free":0}}]}],"trait_type_constraints":[]},"signature":{"is_unsafe":false,"abi":"Rust","is_variadic":false,"inputs":[{"Deduplicated":47}],"output":{"Deduplicated":66}},"src":"Normal","body":"Opaque"},{"def_id":41,"item_meta":{"name":[{"Ident":["core",0]},{"Ident":["intrinsics",0]},{"Ident":["add_with_overflow",0]}],"span":{"Untagged":{"data":{"file_id":34,"beg":{"line":1958,"col":0},"end":{"line":1958,"col":65}},"generated_from_span":null}},"source_text":null,"attr_info":{"attributes":[{"DocComment":" Performs checked integer addition."},{"DocComment":""},{"DocComment":" Note that, unlike most intrinsics, this is safe to call;"},{"DocComment":" it does not require an `unsafe` block."},{"DocComment":" Therefore, implementations must not require the user to uphold"},{"DocComment":" any safety invariants."},{"DocComment":""},{"DocComment":" The stabilized versions of this intrinsic are available on the inte