or_default"},{"DocComment":""},{"DocComment":" # Panics"},{"DocComment":""},{"DocComment":" Panics if the value is an [`Err`], with a panic message including the"},{"DocComment":" passed message, and the content of the [`Err`]."},{"DocComment":""},{"DocComment":""},{"DocComment":" # Examples"},{"DocComment":""},{"DocComment":" ```should_panic"},{"DocComment":" let x: Result<u32, &str> = Err(\"emergency failure\");"},{"DocComment":" x.expect(\"Testing expect\"); // panics with `Testing expect: emergency failure`"},{"DocComment":" ```"},{"DocComment":""},{"DocComment":" # Recommended Message Style"},{"DocComment":""},{"DocComment":" We recommend that `expect` messages are used to describe the reason you"},{"DocComment":" _expect_ the `Result` should be `Ok`."},{"DocComment":""},{"DocComment":" ```should_panic"},{"DocComment":" let path = std::env::var(\"IMPORTANT_PATH\")"},{"DocComment":"     .expect(\"env variable `IMPORTANT_PATH` should be set by `wrapper_script.sh`\");"},{"DocComment":" ```"},{"DocComment":""},{"DocComment":" **Hint**: If you're having trouble remembering how to phrase expect"},{"DocComment":" error messages remember to focus on the word \"should\" as in \"env"},{"DocComment":" variable should be set by blah\" or \"the given binary should be available"},{"DocComment":" and executable by the current user\"."},{"DocComment":""},{"DocComment":" For more detail on expect message styles and the reasoning behind our recommendation please"},{"DocComment":" refer to the section on [\"Common Message"},{"DocComment":" Styles\"](../../std/error/index.html#common-message-styles) in the"},{"DocComment":" [`std::error`](../../std/error/index.html) module docs."},{"Builtin":{"TrackCaller":{"Untagged":{"data":{"file_id":15,"beg":{"line":1176,"col":4},"end":{"line":1176,"col":19}},"generated_from_span":null}}}}],"inline":"Hint","rename":null,"public":true},"is_local":false,"started_from":false,"is_extern":false,"opacity":"Foreign","lang_item":null,"diagnostic_item"